# ─── Never commit these. They hold live tenant data or credentials. ───────────
#
# sweep.py takes a real JWT and calls the QA BFF as a real user. Its input is a
# credential and its output is another tenant's numbers. Neither belongs in git.
*.jwt
*.token
tok.txt
token.txt
sweep-results.json
sweep-*.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── The design deck ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 75 MB of embedded images, and git keeps every version of it forever. Three
# reasons it stays out:
#   - Figma is the canonical source; this is an export of it
#   - everything in it is already transcribed into ontology/ — that was S1
#   - RESOLUTION-POLICY.md ranks the deck BELOW the live API, so committing the
#     lowest-precedence source at the highest storage cost is backwards
#
# If it ever does need versioning, use Git LFS rather than lifting this line:
#   git lfs install && git lfs track "*.docx"
Agency Admin Dashboard*.docx
*.docx

# ─── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ─── Editors and OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─── Scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
scratch/
tmp/
